{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Commissioner Wilson said it is his honor to present this to retired Polk County Sheriff's office K-9, Ace. He thanked his handler and partner Deputy Natalie Oestreich for bringing him here today to recognize the great job he has done. He said it was through Ace's brave action that he saved his partner and two other deputies' lives when the man opened fire on them. He presented them with a plaque for being injured in the line of duty. He said we recognize Ace's brave actions that resulted in serious bodily injury while saving the lives of others. \par
\par
Steve Lester, Chief of Staff, Sheriff's office, said on behalf of Grady Judy and the Sheriff's office they are grateful for the acknowledgement. He said today we are recognizing them for their heroic efforts on that particular moment on that day. He said in a county over 2,000 square miles they are putting their K-9's in harms way every single day. He said they are going into woods, swamps, structures, businesses and attics where they do not know what is around the corner. He said they are doing that in apprehension of murderers, rapists and pedophiles and they do it everyday. He said they are heroes to us and we are grateful to have Ace here with his. He said this commission has continued to make public safety a priority and that is why we have the nations best deputies, K-9's and training. \par
\par
Commissioner Scott said looking at our training facilities and the amount of time every deputy puts into their job he appreciates as a citizen the sacrifice they make every single day. He said oftentimes it is without the support of the community. He said he is thankful we have the best Sheriff's office in the nation and he appreciates the dedication. \par
\par
Chair Santiago said she saw the video on TV and her tears came down. She said we all feel for this and we are glad Ace made it through. She thanked Chief Lester and said to thank the Sheriff for everything they do to put themselves on the line all the time. \par
}

