\par
Commissioner Scott said this represents Polk looking ahead in the future with consolidating and updating operations. He said it seems like we sometimes move slow and specific to Animal Control improvements do happen overtime and we are not sitting here all static and ignoring comments. He said there is stuff that does occur to improve and we cannot move everything simultaneously with a limited budget. He said when you look at items that are a heavy lift budget wise a lot of money goes into the county to serve the residents everyday. He said it is a challenge on how quickly you can make things happen but patience does result in good success. He said this is a project that is a needed asset that will allow them to serve the community.\par
}

