\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 County Manager Bill Beasley discussed the Construction Manager at Risk Agreement 2026-005, Guaranteed Maximum Price Addendum with Rodda Construction, Inc., for the expansion and renovation of the Medical Examiner's office. He said this includes a Hardee County contribution of $500,000, a Highland County contribution of $1.5 million, and a state grant totaling $3 million. He recommended approval. \par
\par
Commissioner Troutman said the difference in the amounts contributed by the counties is based upon amount of work done for each county.\par
\par
Mr. Beasley said they get workload data and the vast majority of autopsies and investigations conducted by the Medical Examiner's office are for Polk County cases.\par
}

