{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Commissioner Troutman said today is election day and she encouraged the audience to vote. She said there has been a lot of discussion on the tax amendment. She said whether it passes or fails, that as a Board and as a community, we have to be realistic that this issue is going to come back. She said once we have a new Board assembled they should talk about ways they can look at the budget and work towards being prepared. She said at some point there is going to be legislation that is going to come down around that. She said for CareerSource Polk and Polk Vision they have set up two days for the Industry and Education Summit. She said on November 12th in Lakeland they are encouraging business and industry leaders to come out and have conversation about educational needs for workforce development.\par
}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Commissioner Wilson said to get out and vote today. He said everybody says this is the most important election we are having. He thanked Chair Santiago and said it will be unusual coming in and she is not here and it will be quieter. \par
}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Commissioner Braswell said we have had 2 children shot recently and one here in Bartow. He said with the three-year old in Bartow the parents gun was there, the kid picked it up and shot himself. He said we cannot be too aware or cautious. He said when you have kids and guns they do not understand what they are, what they mean and what they can do. He said you cannot take a chance with a gun around a kid. He said it is election day and a lot of Republicans vote on election day and are like early voting or mail-in voting is just not good. He said people in Brevard, DeSoto and Highland counties cannot get to the polls because of flooding. He said there is always something that comes up on Election Day and it is a shame and a reality they are living in. He discussed the collective bargaining agreement and said the transition of where they were a few years ago to where they are headed to next year he is glad they are all a part of that. He said they have got them going in the right direction. He said the cancer and stress aspect is important to recognize and deal with as much as the ability to enjoy life with their family. He said he is glad we did it and if we don't do these things we are not going to have the personnel available. He said they are advertising for fire fighters everywhere, it is getting really competitive and we have to stay competitive. He congratulated Chair Santiago. \par
}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Commissioner Scott said to get out and vote. He said he sits on the Canvassing Board and the mail-in votes count and the day of voting counts. He said to get your voice out there and to do that you have to get out and vote. He said to followup on the concerns with the fence warranty and lighting.\par
\par
County Manager Bill Beasley say they did respond to Mr. Abercrombie and the county is working to address all of that. \par
\par
Commissioner Scott said the county will be coming out with an informational flyer for the four-lane widening of Kathleen Road north of Duff Road. \par
}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Chair Santiago said for those who have been speaking on animal welfare issues she wants them to know that their words and comments have not fallen on deaf ears. She said a lot has happened since the beginning and there is more to be done. She is confident that we will continue moving in the right direction. \par
\par
She said she is overwhelmed with the recognition and she wants to thank her fellow commissioners for being by her side and for working together. She said she could not ask for a better Board to work with. She said she will continue working for Polk as a private citizen. She looks forward to seeing all the good things that will happen in our county because of the good people we have. \par
\par
Meeting adjourned at 11:12 a.m.\par
